#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198057 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198415 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83edde2a-daa5-50ce-b48c-3ded50a1a179" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "985e1b18-0023-55ba-b4e4-69a109d8de58" :question/math-academy-id "e-12485" :question/problem "![](images/04/0405639a97f249bbcc4dc18a7eae5b4df24aefb4b4680b569365b3d841c15e6b.png)\n\n   \n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $y$-axis and the lines $x=\\dfrac{y}2$ and $x=y-2$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda(x,y) =\\dfrac y8.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\:\\: 2x \\leq y \\leq x+2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/69/69dcf02cc1883f2b04f81bd6dd486bbe24fedbb813db5778ae3b33ed1fb42e90.png)\n\n     \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}(\\frac{y}{8})(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{\\int }_{2x}^{x+2}\\frac{y}{8}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}]}_{2x}^{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x-2)^{2}((x+2)^{2}-(2x)^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-4x+4)(4+4x-3{x}^{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(16-24{x}^{2}+16{x}^{3}-3{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}{[16x-8{x}^{3}+4{x}^{4}-\\frac{3{x}^{5}}{5}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(32-64+64-\\frac{96}{5})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{16}(\\frac{64}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198058 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198416 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7321a6d4-007e-5813-bfa7-9e06d0789358" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/id #uuid "eab955a5-019b-5219-b5d5-32e3818be4b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-12486" :question/problem "![](images/67/67d511da69c49e77822011936522f2b236ccc0fa0e0fcd09ce26b428cc8f738a.png)\n\n \n\nA plate with mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region $D$ enclosed between the curves $y=x$ and $y=4x-x^2$, as shown above. Given that the region has an area of $\\dfrac92$ square units, find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3, \\:\\: x \\leq y \\leq 4x-x^2 \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/62/6291950b5483f3c102df7249674412c7c11646409cb1b43df604de6bd5ace86f.png)\n\n  \n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=3$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x - 3|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = \\dfrac{M}{\\mathcal{A}} = \\dfrac{2M}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}|x-3{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{x}^{4x-{x}^{2}}(x-3)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(x-3)^{2}[y]_{y=x}^{y=4x-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}({x}^{2}-6x+9)(3x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{\\int }_{0}^{3}-{x}^{4}+9{x}^{3}-27{x}^{2}+27x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{9}{[-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{9{x}^{4}}{4}-9{x}^{3}+\\frac{27{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{{3}^{2}}(-\\frac{{3}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{{3}^{6}}{4}-{3}^{5}+\\frac{{3}^{5}}{2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot {3}^{3}M(-\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{27M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198060 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198418 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/id #uuid "0f7dbe9f-b448-5e76-9932-68e1ff99904e" :question/math-academy-id "e-12488" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8ec9b8832f3286032413c4016e88a58a593dfd1b32164e219dc1c2e56e3b0b97.png)\n\nA plate with mass $M$ occupies the region $D$ in the first quadrant enclosed between the curve $y=\\sqrt x$ and the line $x=1,$ as shown above. \nThe mass density at each point is proportional to its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\nI_l = \\iint\\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) [r(x,y)]^2 \\:\\textrm{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda(x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq \\sqrt x \\right\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/7f/7faaecf39250dbdd1b92d789f6c217afe883c27533b563dae82ed82d228d9b4d.png)\n\nAlso, the distance between a point and the line $x=-1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y) = |x-(-1)| = |x+1|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda(x,y) = k |y| = ky,$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}ky\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = k y = 4M y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My\\,|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}4My(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}y\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x+1)^{2}(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2M{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2M(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =2M\\cdot \\frac{17}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{17M}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198649 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198418 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4820138b-483c-5ced-8df9-9849f5f2a7cb" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia Given a Description of a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa382cb2-c023-5ce5-885a-e1b72b5790e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2M}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194526} {:answer/id #uuid "d548c7eb-c1fb-5fe3-9e43-4760ac006cbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194527} {:answer/id #uuid "001dd569-8891-54f9-9dd6-95c9c954b57e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2M" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194528} {:answer/id #uuid "034ffee4-a514-54a1-8af5-fa58f01a0c7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{M}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194529} {:answer/id #uuid "40eef011-60c1-5f0d-bd81-34a57693cad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3M}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194530}] :answer-field/id #uuid "2201e78f-496f-5433-9cbb-1e1b8cd49bb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194525}] :question/id #uuid "c50ed432-0fe6-5819-a38a-01c1c51de9fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-163007" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D = {(x, y): - 1 \\le x \\le 2, 0 \\le y \\le 3}$.\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y = 3$."}]}
